put.gd package dependency notice

Licences. The package's licence metadata names the main licences: MIT (put.gd),
Apache-2.0 (the AWS SDK for C++) and, with the Proton Drive helper, GPL-3.0-or-later
(Proton's crypto). This file lists every licence of the code the package contains:

  put.gd                                    MIT                 LICENSE
  IBM Plex Sans Regular, Medium, SemiBold    OFL-1.1             fonts/OFL-sans.txt
  IBM Plex Mono Regular                     OFL-1.1             fonts/OFL-mono.txt
  zkde-screencast-unstable-v1 bindings      LGPL-2.1-or-later   wayland-zkde-screencast-unstable-v1.xml
    (in putgd-record)
  ext/wlr data-control-v1 bindings          MIT-style           wayland-*-data-control-*.xml
  AWS SDK for C++, aws-crt-cpp, aws-c-*,    Apache-2.0          aws-*-LICENSE, aws-*-NOTICE
    s2n-tls
  cJSON, libcbor (in the AWS libraries)     MIT                 aws-sdk-cJSON-LICENSE,
                                                                aws-crt-cpp-crt-aws-c-common-THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES
  xxHash (in the AWS libraries)             BSD-2-Clause        aws-crt-cpp-crt-aws-checksums-xxHash-LICENSE
  TinyXML-2 (in the AWS libraries)          Zlib                aws-sdk-TinyXML2-LICENSE
  Proton Drive helper, when included:                           proton/
    Proton Drive SDK and account code       MIT                 proton/LICENSE.proton
    Proton crypto (WebPackages)             GPL-3.0-or-later    proton/LICENSE.crypto-GPL-3.0
    OpenPGP.js                              LGPL-3.0-or-later   proton/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt
    bcryptjs                                BSD-3-Clause        proton/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt
    other bundled npm packages              MIT                 proton/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt
    Bun runtime                             MIT                 proton/BUN-*
    JavaScriptCore/WebKit (in Bun)          LGPL-2.0-or-later   proton/BUN-THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.gz
    TinyCC (in Bun)                         LGPL-2.1-or-later   proton/BUN-THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.gz

Qt 6 and QtKeychain are dynamically linked distribution packages. Their licenses,
source and security updates are supplied through the distribution package manager.
Qt platform plugins and SQLite SQL driver remain distribution owned.

The official AWS SDK for C++ and its CRT shared libraries are privately installed
under the putgd library directory. Pinned source identities are recorded in
/usr/share/putgd/dependency-lock.json. AWS SDK and CRT Apache-2.0 license texts
(aws-*-LICENSE) and their NOTICE files (aws-*-NOTICE) are installed alongside this
notice; s2n-tls uses Apache-2.0. The SDK and CRT libraries also contain cJSON (MIT,
aws-sdk-cJSON-LICENSE), TinyXML-2 (Zlib, aws-sdk-TinyXML2-LICENSE), libcbor (MIT,
aws-crt-cpp-crt-aws-c-common-THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES) and xxHash (BSD-2-Clause,
aws-crt-cpp-crt-aws-checksums-xxHash-LICENSE). Rebuild the pinned official
SDK following docs/build.md, update the lock deliberately, and rebuild the DEB to
update these libraries. No compiler or Qt runtime is bundled.

The ext-data-control-v1, wlr-data-control-unstable-v1 and zkde-screencast-unstable-v1
Wayland protocol notices are retained in wayland-ext-data-control-v1.xml,
wayland-wlr-data-control-unstable-v1.xml and wayland-zkde-screencast-unstable-v1.xml
beside this file, including their original copyright and license text. Generated
client bindings use those protocols.

When the package includes the Proton Drive helper (/usr/libexec/putgd/proton), its
licenses, the notices of everything compiled into it and the list of its
corresponding source are in the proton directory beside this file.

Source. put.gd's own source and the helper's corresponding source (Proton's crypto,
OpenPGP.js, and Bun with JavaScriptCore and TinyCC, with the rebuild instructions)
are published with this release at
@PUTGD_SOURCE_URL@
as putgd-VERSION-source.tar.gz, putgd-proton-corresponding-source.tar.gz.part1
and .part2 (concatenate them) and proton-source-catalog.json. proton/SOURCES.json
lists the source packets by SHA-256, and proton/SOURCE-LOCATION.txt repeats this.

Native packages include desktop integration assets and dependency notices. Release
artifacts have build identities, package inventories and published checksums. Verify
these against the exact artifact being installed. Installation and artifact auditing
alone do not certify compositor support or install/upgrade/removal behavior; consult
https://github.com/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/blob/main/docs/verification.md
and https://github.com/patrick-hudson/put.gd-desktop/blob/main/docs/release.md
for tested versions and remaining gates, including the complete release license audit.
